{
  "id": "fs-electric",
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "name": "FS Electric (generic)",
  "description": "Formula Student electric car to make your own: typical values, not a real car (typical — replace with your data). 280 kg with driver; one rear E-Motor (230 N·m, about 100 kW) through a 4.4 chain drive and an open differential; front wheels unpowered, with brakes; Accumulator 138s4p, 580 V full, 7.2 kWh, 0.3 Ω, with the battery's Formula Student Electric preset; CG height 0.28 m, wheelbase 1.53 m, CdA 1.2 m², CzA 3.0 m² (45 % front); tyres μ 1.5 with a load sensitivity of −0.2 per kN.\nRules, FS Rules 2026 v1.1 (FSG): 80 kW at the accumulator outlet (EV 2.2.1), judged on a 500 ms moving average (D 10.4.1); 500 A (EV 2.2.2, not modelled); 600 V DC (EV 4.1.1); 75 m acceleration (D 5.1.1) staged 0.3 m behind the line (D 5.2.4); the 25 s limit for driverless runs only (D 9.2.1); endurance about 22 km (D 7.1.3). FSUK and FSAE may differ: check the current season's rules.\nWhat to expect (estimates):\n• Acceleration 75 m: 3.74 s from the start line, 119 km/h at the line, 0–100 km/h in 2.93 s, held at 80 kW for 3.8 s (FS Czech Republic 2025, 35 EV teams: 3.51–6.44 s, median 3.91 s, the case's reference time)\n• Autocross (flying lap): 57.7 s on LightSim's own 979 m layout\n• Endurance energy: 23 laps (22.5 km) with the Output Power Limit at 30 kW, a typical endurance setting, and no driver change: 5.33 kWh net at the accumulator, 18 % of it recuperated, 25 % SOC left, 473–594 V (FS Czech Republic 2025 efficiency, 14 scored teams: 3.19–6.15 kWh, median 5.25 kWh)\nSweep: on Acceleration 75 m, sweep Accumulator · Output Power Limit from 40 to 80 in 5 steps: 4.22 s at 40 kW to 3.74 s at 80 kW.",
